MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Revolver and Rubber Soul feel like natural next choices because I listened to Sgt. Pepper and want to explore more Beatles music.",
    "The Beach Boys and Elvis collections fit my repeated interest in older songs and greatest-hits compilations, while A Very Special Christmas 2 directly follows my recent Christmas listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Best of INXS and Adele 21 are less compelling right now because I am mainly drawn to Beatles albums, mid-'60s music, and a follow-up to my recent Christmas album.",
    "Duets and Shadowland give me too little information to connect them confidently to what I want; the title Duets alone does not establish the connection I enjoyed with Cheek to Cheek."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A greatest-hits format helps, but it does not make every collection equally appealing: the Beach Boys fit my current interests more closely than INXS.",
    "My listening to Born This Way does not mean newer pop is a priority on every visit, so Adele 21 feels like too broad a leap."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent interaction with A Very Special Christmas makes its direct follow-up especially relevant to what I want now.",
    "The combination of Sgt. Pepper, AM Gold: The Mid-'60s, and older hits collections matters more to me than a broad connection to pop or rock."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations capture my interest in older music and familiar hits, but some stretch that interest beyond the Beatles, mid-'60s songs, and Christmas follow-up I currently favor."
}
